{
 "#": "OpenGL and Vulkan frames through Direct3D 11 (run.py --cases gfx-gl-interop,gfx-vk-interop --expect expect/gfx_interop.json, with the stand-in's default script: D3D11 alone): the session is D3D11, and the test pattern of gfx-gl-basic and gfx-vk-basic shows as it does on their own APIs. Skipped without an OpenGL or Vulkan driver (and so on CI). The bounds cases (gfx-gl-interop-bounds, gfx-vk-interop-bounds) show what gfx-gl-bounds and gfx-vk-bounds show: an OpenGL texture's v counts from its bottom row there too. gfx-gl-interop-odd: OpenGL slice 1 of two-slice arrays (SubmitWithArrayIndex: the other eye's pattern), a two-slice array of eye 0's pattern with Submit_GlArrayTexture (the left eye slice 0, the right slice 1), a 4x multisampled texture, a renderbuffer, a 4x multisampled renderbuffer and a renderbuffer with flipped bounds (upside down), each its own size; all the right way up. gfx-vk-interop-odd: Vulkan slice 1 of two-slice arrays through SubmitWithArrayIndex and through Submit_VulkanTextureWithArrayData (the other eye's pattern). gfx-vk-interop-gpu-wait: a game whose device has the extensions GetVulkanDeviceExtensionsRequired names (semaphores_asked: VK_KHR_external_semaphore_win32 among them), its copies waited for on the GPU; shown as the basic case.",
